      "writtenOn": "2022-06-22T01:55:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I thought it might be useful for future use in the PD stack itself since it currently treats this message type as an array of uint16_t\u0027s, which is wrong since the last field is a uint8_t, it\u0027s hard to read, and assumes a LE processor anyways. I\u0027d solve the endianness problem by using Zephyr\u0027s byteorder macros when accessing the struct members (https://docs.zephyrproject.org/apidoc/latest/byteorder_8h.html#ae4176f3e082f21488dedcd02b406cb43) so it\u0027d be like using htons() in the unix sockets API\n\n(Struct has since moved to https://crrev.com/c/3715697)",
